Rule 1 (input tensor is well-formed for ones_like)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (valid when dtype is omitted; tensor has non-negative dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (explicit dtype matches the input’s dtype — always valid)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : dtype} |= v_2 = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 5 (dtype must be a recognized TensorFlow/NumPy dtype code: 0–10)
{v_2 : dtype} |= v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5 ∨ v_2 = 6 ∨ v_2 = 7 ∨ v_2 = 8 ∨ v_2 = 9 ∨ v_2 = 10
>>
Rule 6 (dtype may match the input tensor’s dtype or be any recognized dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : dtype} |= v_2 = dtype_(v_1) ∨ (v_2 = 0 ∨ v_2 = 1 ∨ v_2 = 2 ∨ v_2 = 3 ∨ v_2 = 4 ∨ v_2 = 5 ∨ v_2 = 6 ∨ v_2 = 7 ∨ v_2 = 8 ∨ v_2 = 9 ∨ v_2 = 10)
>>
Rule 7 (input tensor has a valid, non-negative shape for all dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 8 (dtype cannot be a string code or meta-dtype)
{v_2 : dtype} |= v_2 ≠ 11 ∧ v_2 ≠ 12
